   "why_the_registered_metric_cannot_score_v2": "It counts clips whose duration_s exceeds 30s. duration_s is len(audio)/16000 in both backends (asr.py:202, asr.py:260), so it describes the audio file and not the pipeline: it returns the same 92 under v1, under v2, and under any future decoder. It was an exact proxy in v1 only because WhisperProcessor truncated unconditionally at n_samples=480000, so every long clip was necessarily cut. Once chunking exists the proxy stops tracking the defect. The flaw is in our pre-registered design, and is recorded here rather than worked around silently.",
